{
  "schema_version": "fabric.node-prevalidate-vectors/v1",
  "rule": "Spec 050 §3.14 (R10, OD-1): fabriccontent runs the stateless checks on every content record before acknowledging it, in order: the descriptor rules (schema, role table, protection, links) -> bad_descriptor; body length and sha256 against the descriptor -> digest_mismatch; allowed_tenants -> tenant_not_allowed; the source binding -> source_unbound; for a stored record.evidence body the envelope check of §3.4a item 4 -> evidence_not_canonical, evidence_envelope, evidence_type_unregistered or evidence_bounds. A refusal is a permanent error the OTLP receiver answers with HTTP 400; nothing is enqueued and fabric_content_prevalidate_refused{reason} counts it. accepted means every stateless check passed and the record is queued, never that it is durable; the store-conflict check stays after acknowledgement. Bodies are base64; the over-cap body is generated (body_repeat: one byte repeated).",
  "reasons": [
    "bad_descriptor",
    "digest_mismatch",
    "tenant_not_allowed",
    "source_unbound",
    "evidence_not_canonical",
    "evidence_envelope",
    "evidence_type_unregistered",
    "evidence_bounds"
  ],
  "config": {
    "allowed_tenants": [
      "tenant-a"
    ],
    "source_binding": {
      "tenant_id": "tenant-a",
      "source_id": "wire-3f9a1c2b7d4e5f60"
    }
  },
  "registered_evidence_types": [
